"[2509.09255v1] Sensible Agent: A Framework for Unobtrusive Interaction with Proactive AR Agents (https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.09255v1)\nciteturn29794view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.09255v1\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 161\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Human-Computer Interaction\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 11 Sep 2025 (this version), latest version 30 Oct 2025 (cite5†v2 )]\nL9: # Title:Sensible Agent: A Framework for Unobtrusive Interaction with Proactive AR Agents\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite6†Geonsun Lee , cite7†Min Xia , cite8†Nels Numan , cite9†Xun Qian , cite10†David Li , cite11†Yanhe Chen , cite12†Achin Kulshrestha , cite13†Ishan Chatterjee , cite14†Yinda Zhang , cite15†Dinesh Manocha , cite16†David Kim , cite17†Ruofei Du L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled Sensible Agent: A Framework for Unobtrusive Interaction with Proactive AR Agents, by Geonsun Lee and 11 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite18†View PDF cite19†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:Proactive AR agents promise context-aware assistance, but their interactions often rely on explicit voice prompts or responses, which can be disruptive or socially awkward. We introduce Sensible Agent, a framework designed for unobtrusive interaction with these proactive agents. Sensible Agent dynamically adapts both \"what\" assistance to offer and, crucially, \"how\" to deliver it, based on real-time multimodal context sensing.\nL17: Informed by an expert workshop (n=12) and a data annotation study (n=40), the framework leverages egocentric cameras, multimodal sensing, and Large Multimodal Models (LMMs) to infer context and suggest appropriate actions delivered via minimally intrusive interaction modes. We demonstrate our prototype on an XR headset through a user study (n=10) in both AR and VR scenarios.\nL18: Results indicate that Sensible Agent significantly reduces perceived interaction effort compared to voice-prompted baseline, while maintaining high usability and achieving higher preference.\nL19: Subjects:  | Human-Computer Interaction (cs.HC)\nL20: Cite as:  | cite20†arXiv:2509.09255 [cs.HC]\nL21:    | (or cite21†arXiv:2509.09255v1 [cs.HC] for this version)\nL22:    | cite22†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2509.09255†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL23: Related DOI (Digital Object Identifier):  | cite23†https://doi.org/10.1145/3746059.3747748†doi.org DOI(s) linking to related resources\nL24: ## Submission history\nL25: \nL26: From: Geonsun Lee [cite24†view email ]\nL27: [v1] Thu, 11 Sep 2025 08:40:26 UTC (26,825 KB)\nL28: cite5†[v2] Thu, 30 Oct 2025 19:39:46 UTC (26,825 KB)\nL29: \nL30: Full-text links:\nL31: \nL32: ## Access Paper:\nL33: \nL34: View a PDF of the paper titled Sensible Agent: A Framework for Unobtrusive Interaction with Proactive AR Agents, by Geonsun Lee and 11 other authors\nL35: \nL36:   * cite18†View PDF L37:   * cite19†HTML (experimental) L38:   * cite25†TeX Source L39: \nL40: cite26†view license†creativecommons.org L41: ### Current browse context:\nL42: \nL43: cs.HC\nL44: \nL45: cite27†< prev |   cite28†next > L46: \nL47: cite29†new | cite30†recent | cite31†2025-09 L48: \nL49: Change to browse by:\nL50: \nL51: cite32†cs L52: \nL53: ### References & Citations\nL54: \nL55:   * cite33†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L56:   * cite34†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L57:   * cite35†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org L58: \nL59: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL60: \nL61: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL62: \nL63: [Button: ×]\nL64: \nL65: loading...\nL66: \nL67: Data provided by:\nL68: \nL69: ### Bookmar